// Empirically recover the TMA 128B-swizzle layout for a [128,128] K-major bf16 tile loaded as
// two 64-col boxes (box0 -> sK[0..8192), box1 -> sK[8192..16384)), matching tma_swz_test.
// Probe1: K[mn,k] = k  -> for each smem offset e, which head-dim k landed there.
// Probe2: K[mn,k] = mn -> for each smem offset e, which row mn landed there.
// Combine to get full perm (mn,k) -> e, then compare against candidate formulas.
//   nvcc -O3 -std=c++17 -gencode arch=compute_90a,code=sm_90a tma_probe.cu -lcuda -o /tmp/tma_probe && /tmp/tma_probe
#include "oracle_common.cuh"
#include <cuda.h>
#include <vector>
